IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore Food Agency Act 2019 (Singapore) -- the Agency's symbol (s 8), membership, disqualification, term, resignation and
-- vacation of office (ss 9, 11, 12, 16, 18, 20), quorum and voting (ss 23, 25), secrecy (s 34), protection from personal liability
-- (s 35), borrowing (s 42), misuse of accreditation, certification or inspection marks (s 43), composition (s 44) and the liability
-- of officers for a corporation's offence (s 45(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SFAA2019.txt. The revised
-- edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the body is
-- S 26/2022 (wef 13 January 2022, s 11(2)(d)). The deposit's metadata labels it "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. It is an institutional Act: it sets up the
-- Agency and leaves food safety itself to the Acts it administers. SCOPED to the rules with decision content. Not encoded: the
-- functions and powers (ss 5, 6), Ministerial directions (s 7), appointment instruments (s 10), acting appointments (s 14),
-- validity of acts (s 17), presiding (s 24), execution of documents (s 26), committees and delegation (ss 27 to 30), personnel
-- (ss 31 to 33), finance other than borrowing (ss 36 to 41), offences by unincorporated associations (s 46, which mirrors s 45),
-- service (s 47), regulations (s 48), and the transfer and transitional Parts 8 and 9.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore Food Agency Act 2019 -- the Agency`

-- helpers
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the later of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `8 -- the Agency's symbol`

-- s 8(2): a person who "(a) uses, without the prior written permission of the Agency, a symbol or representation identical with the
-- Agency's symbol or representation; or (b) uses a symbol or representation which so resembles the Agency's symbol or
-- representation as to deceive or cause confusion, or to be likely to deceive or to cause confusion" commits an offence: fine up to
-- $10,000 or imprisonment up to 6 months or both. Limb (b) carries no permission exception in the text.
DECLARE SymbolUse IS ONE OF
    `an identical symbol`
    `a confusingly similar symbol`
    `a dissimilar symbol`

GIVEN `the use` IS A SymbolUse, `has prior written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the symbol use is an offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `an identical symbol` THEN NOT `has prior written permission`
    WHEN `a confusingly similar symbol` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `9, 12 -- membership`

-- s 9(1): "The Agency consists of at least 7 and not more than 14 members." (2) "One of the members (who is not the Chairperson) may
-- be the Chief Executive." s 12(1)(a): the Chairperson is "a member (other than the Chief Executive)".
GIVEN `number of members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the membership size is lawful` IF
    `number of members` AT LEAST 7 AND `number of members` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `is the Chief Executive` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be appointed Chairperson` IF
    `is a member` AND (NOT `is the Chief Executive`)

§§ `11(2) -- disqualification`

-- s 11(2): disqualified are (a) "an undischarged bankrupt or an individual who has an arrangement with any of his or her creditors";
-- (b) "a Judge or judicial officer"; (c) "an individual who has been sentenced to imprisonment for a term of 6 months or more, and
-- has not received a free pardon"; (d) one disqualified as a company or VCC director under the Companies Act 1967 or the Variable
-- Capital Companies Act 2018, during the disqualification; (e) one who lacks capacity under the Mental Capacity Act 2008 or is the
-- subject of an order under s 10 of the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) Act 2008.
DECLARE Candidate HAS
    `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a Judge or judicial officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER
    `has received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is disqualified as a company or VCC director` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lacks capacity` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is disqualified` IF
        `the candidate`'s `is an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `has an arrangement with creditors`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `is a Judge or judicial officer`
    OR  (`the candidate`'s `months of imprisonment sentenced` AT LEAST 6 AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `has received a free pardon`))
    OR  `the candidate`'s `is disqualified as a company or VCC director`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `lacks capacity`

§§ `16, 18 -- term and resignation`

-- s 18(1): "each member of the Agency holds office for a period of 3 years or any shorter period specified in the instrument of
-- appointment." (2) "A member of the Agency may be re-appointed." Months are used here; 0 means no period specified.
GIVEN `months specified in the instrument` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the term of office in months` MEANS
    IF `months specified in the instrument` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the lower of` `months specified in the instrument` 36
    ELSE 36

-- s 16(2): "The resignation is effective when the notice in subsection (1) is received by the Minister or at any later time
-- specified in the notice." Days are counted from any common origin; 0 means no time specified.
GIVEN `day the Minister receives the notice` IS A NUMBER, `day specified in the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day the resignation takes effect` MEANS
    `the later of` `day the Minister receives the notice` `day specified in the notice`

§§ `20 -- vacation of office`

-- s 20(1): a member ceases to hold office if he or she (a) dies; (b) is adjudicated a bankrupt or makes an arrangement with
-- creditors; (c) becomes otherwise disqualified under s 11(2); (d) is removed under s 15; (e) resigns under s 16; (f) "without
-- reasonable cause, fails to disclose any interest" required under the Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018 "and a notice is given
-- under that Act to the Minister about that default"; (g) "fails to attend 3 consecutive meetings of the Agency without the approval
-- of the Agency"; or (h) is not re-appointed when the term expires. (2): no compensation for ceasing to hold office.
DECLARE Member HAS
    `has died` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is adjudicated bankrupt or has an arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has become otherwise disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been removed by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has resigned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `failed without reasonable cause to disclose an interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice of the default given to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consecutive meetings missed without approval` IS A NUMBER
    `term expired without re-appointment` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member has vacated office` IF
        `the member`'s `has died`
    OR  `the member`'s `is adjudicated bankrupt or has an arrangement`
    OR  `the member`'s `has become otherwise disqualified`
    OR  `the member`'s `has been removed by the Minister`
    OR  `the member`'s `has resigned`
    OR  (`the member`'s `failed without reasonable cause to disclose an interest` AND `the member`'s `notice of the default given to the Minister`)
    OR  `the member`'s `consecutive meetings missed without approval` AT LEAST 3
    OR  `the member`'s `term expired without re-appointment`

§§ `23, 25 -- quorum and voting`

-- s 23(1): "The quorum is the number that is one-third the number of members of the Agency." (2) "No business may be transacted at a
-- meeting of the Agency if a quorum is not present." The text does not say how a fraction is rounded; this encoding treats a quorum
-- as present when at least one-third of the members attend (INFERENCE).
GIVEN `number of members` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a quorum is present` IF
    `members present` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `number of members`

-- s 25(1) one vote each; (2) the presiding member has "in the case of an equality of votes, a casting vote"; (3) "A resolution of
-- the Agency is passed if it is agreed by all members present without dissent, or if a majority of the members who are entitled to
-- vote on the matter cast votes in favour of it." (4) a member present "is presumed to have agreed to, and to have voted in favour
-- of" a resolution unless he or she expressly dissents or votes against it (or is barred by s 26 of the Public Sector (Governance)
-- Act 2018). So every present member who does not dissent is counted in favour. The casting vote is treated here as one extra vote
-- in favour, and the majority test is then applied (INFERENCE: s 25 does not say how (2) and (3) combine).
GIVEN `members present and entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER, `members expressly dissenting` IS A NUMBER, `members entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER, `presiding member casts in favour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the resolution is passed` IF
        `members expressly dissenting` EQUALS 0
    OR  `effective votes in favour` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `members entitled to vote`
    WHERE
        `votes in favour` MEANS `members present and entitled to vote` MINUS `members expressly dissenting`
        `casting vote` MEANS
            IF `votes in favour` EQUALS `members expressly dissenting` AND `presiding member casts in favour`
            THEN 1
            ELSE 0
        `effective votes in favour` MEANS `votes in favour` PLUS `casting vote`

GIVEN `number of members` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER, `members expressly dissenting` IS A NUMBER, `presiding member casts in favour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agency validly resolves` IF
        `a quorum is present` `number of members` `members present`
    AND `the resolution is passed` `members present` `members expressly dissenting` `number of members` `presiding member casts in favour`

§§ `34 -- secrecy`

-- s 34(1): a member, employee, delegate or subdelegate, the Chief Executive or a committee member "who has information in his or her
-- capacity as such that would not otherwise be available to him or her, must not disclose that information to any person except"
-- (a) in performing the Agency's functions; (b) with the Agency's prior authorisation; (c) for proceedings for an offence under the
-- Act or a report of them; (d) as required by a court order; (e) in disclosing interests as the Act requires; (f) as required or
-- allowed by or under this or any other Act. (2): fine up to $2,000 or imprisonment up to 12 months or both.
DECLARE DisclosurePurpose IS ONE OF
    `performing the Agency's functions`
    `with the Agency's prior authorisation`
    `proceedings for an offence under the Act`
    `a court order`
    `disclosing interests as the Act requires`
    `required or allowed by written law`
    `a press interview`
    `helping a friend's business`

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A DisclosurePurpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is excepted` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `a press interview` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `helping a friend's business` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `is an Agency insider` IS A BOOLEAN, `information obtained only in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN, `the purpose` IS A DisclosurePurpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence` IF
    `is an Agency insider` AND `information obtained only in that capacity` AND (NOT `the purpose is excepted` `the purpose`)

§§ `35 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 35: "No liability shall lie" against a member, committee member, the Chief Executive, an employee, delegate or subdelegate "or
-- any other person acting under the direction of the Agency, for anything which is done or purported to be done, or omitted to be
-- done, in good faith and with reasonable care" in exercising a power or performing a function under this Act.
GIVEN `acting for or under the direction of the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN, `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN, `exercising a power or function under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is protected from personal liability` IF
    `acting for or under the direction of the Agency` AND `in good faith` AND `with reasonable care` AND `exercising a power or function under the Act`

§§ `42 -- borrowing`

-- s 42(1): the Agency "cannot raise loans ... except in accordance with this section". (3): loans may be raised "(a) from the
-- Government; or (b) with the approval of the Minister, from another source, whether within or outside Singapore." (2)(c):
-- debentures, bonds or other instruments "as the Minister may approve".
DECLARE Lender IS ONE OF
    `the Government`
    `a Singapore bank`
    `a lender outside Singapore`

GIVEN `the lender` IS A Lender, `Minister has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agency may borrow` IF
    CONSIDER `the lender`
    WHEN `the Government` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `Minister has approved`

§§ `43 -- accreditation, certification and inspection marks`

-- s 43(1): a person must not use an accreditation, certification or inspection mark, "or a colourable imitation" of one, unless the
-- person "(a) holds a valid accreditation or certification authorising" that use, or "(b) is authorised by the Agency". (2) no
-- misleading use of a report or certificate; (3) no forging or unauthorised altering. (4) "without reasonable excuse": fine up to
-- $50,000 or imprisonment up to 3 years or both. (5) a District Court may impose the full penalty. (6) forfeiture of property.
GIVEN `uses the mark or a colourable imitation` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a valid accreditation or certification for that use` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised by the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mark use is an offence` IF
        `uses the mark or a colourable imitation`
    AND (NOT `holds a valid accreditation or certification for that use`)
    AND (NOT `authorised by the Agency`)
    AND (NOT `has a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `8, 34, 43 penalties and 44 composition`

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `misusing the Agency's symbol`
    `unlawful disclosure`
    `misusing an accreditation mark`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Agency's symbol` THEN 10000
    WHEN `unlawful disclosure` THEN 2000
    WHEN `misusing an accreditation mark` THEN 50000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `misusing the Agency's symbol` THEN 6
    WHEN `unlawful disclosure` THEN 12
    WHEN `misusing an accreditation mark` THEN 36

-- s 44(1): the Chief Executive or an authorised employee "may compound any offence under this Act that is prescribed as a
-- compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum not exceeding the lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine
-- that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $2,000." Which offences are prescribed is left to regulations (not deposited); the flag
-- stands in for that. 0 means the offence cannot be compounded.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    IF `prescribed as compoundable`
    THEN `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 2000
    ELSE 0

§§ `45(2) -- officers of a corporation`

-- s 45(2): where a corporation commits an offence under the Act, a person "(a) who is (i) an officer of the corporation; or (ii) an
-- individual who is involved in the management of the corporation and in a position to influence the conduct of the corporation"
-- and "(b) who (i) consented or connived, or conspired with others ...; (ii) is ... knowingly concerned in, or is party to, the
-- commission of the offence ...; or (iii) knew or ought reasonably to have known that the offence ... would be or is being committed,
-- and failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent or stop" it, is guilty of the same offence. (5): "whether or not the corporation
-- is convicted of the offence". (3): the person may rely on the corporation's defences with the same burden.
DECLARE Person HAS
    `is an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in management and able to influence the conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consented, connived or conspired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was knowingly concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or ought to have known` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the corporation committed an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of the same offence` IF
        `the corporation committed an offence under the Act`
    AND (`the person`'s `is an officer` OR `the person`'s `is in management and able to influence the conduct`)
    AND (    `the person`'s `consented, connived or conspired`
         OR  `the person`'s `was knowingly concerned`
         OR  (`the person`'s `knew or ought to have known` AND (NOT `the person`'s `took all reasonable steps to prevent it`)))
